//! Roc Platform ABI
//!
//! The Rust interface to a Roc platform, generated by the `RustGlue.roc` glue
//! spec. Do not edit it: regenerate it with `roc glue`.
//!
//! Glue input fingerprint (SHA-256): 1fb702711e9f8c47dc86fbb3f2585ce36655402390f8121226c7cdf9ca21853d
//! It covers the type table, hosted functions and provided entrypoints the
//! spec read, and changes exactly when they do; unchanged input regenerates
//! this file byte for byte. Nothing links against it yet.
//!
//! Ownership:
//! - A Roc value the host holds is one owned reference. A type the host can
//!   release implements `Drop`, and `Clone` adds a reference.
//! - Roc transfers ownership of refcounted arguments to the hosted function.
//!   Dropping one releases it; moving it into storage or into the result keeps it.
//! - Passing a value to Roc moves it: Roc takes the reference.
//! - A value holding an opaque Roc value has no `Drop`, because only Roc can
//!   release it: hand it back to Roc.
//!
//! Import this module from the platform host. Define the six runtime symbols, by
//! hand or through `roc_runtime!`, and implement the hosted symbols declared in
//! `raw` with exactly those natural C ABI signatures.

